From 90d0bcc9def087aff28ea98673c4ff3d7b39ac28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:35:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 176/176] Let Appearance turn animations back on when rendering
 on the CPU

The QEMU profile turns animations off when the launcher renders on the
CPU, and Omarchy 4.5's toggle could not lift that: it said animations
were enabled while they stayed off. As Omarchy does upstream, turning them
on in a CPU session now leaves the animations-without-gpu flag, and the
profile keeps them on while it is there, in later sessions too. The toggle
and the Appearance menu go by Hyprland's real state, so a choice in
looknfeel.lua still wins and the notification says what happened. GPU
rendering is unchanged. Runtime 4.5.0-15 carries the toggle and
compatibility revision 69 refreshes untouched QEMU profiles.
